<title>UK: TI Group stake being placed at 532p-traders.</title>
<headline>TI Group stake being placed at 532p-traders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 42 million shares in engineering company TI Group Plc, equivalent to eight percent of its stock, were being placed in the market early on Wednesday at 532p, market sources said.  </p>
<p>The stake, said to be owned by Germany's Mannesmann, was being placed by brokers UBS, SBC Warburg and Cazenove, according to market sources.</p>
<p>No one at those three brokerages was immediately available for comment. TI shares were down 5-1/2p at 559 by 0744 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
